xt day something  would happen that would make it  strangely apparent i'm supposed to keep  doing this a bit longer  for larson the turnaround started when  she was cast as kate on united states of  terra and drew critical praise for her  performance as the sardonic teenager by  the time the show was canceled after  three seasons  larson's star was on the rise and  casting directors had started taking  note  you want to take a picture with me bree  versus the world  of all the movies she's made larson has  said there's only one she rewatches  the wacky action comedy scott pilgrim vs  the world unfortunately her turn as  ex-girlfriend envy adams went largely  unnoticed by theater goers during its  2010 release  still things were slowly picking up for  larsen she had better luck in her  supporting role as jonah hill's love  interest in 21 jump street which was not  only critically well received it was a  hit at the box office as well  taking in more than 200 million dollars  worldwide larson garnered praise from  critics as a standout who brought nuance  and depth to a supporting character that  could have been totally unmemorable  dramatic breakthrough she may have been  only 23 when she stepped into her first  leaning role as troubled youth care  worker grace in the 2013  indie drama short term 12 but larson had  been working hard for more than 15 years  by the time she got her first major big  screen break  larson shadowed real workers and did  extensive research to capture grace's  emotions with depth and accuracy  she told new york magazine i was  terrified and excited it was confusing  when we screened the film at the south  by southwest festival for the first time  i had never had people look at me that  way before the film won the narrative  feature award at south by southwest  and larson took home a gotham award at  the end of the year  the lighter side larson isn't all about  drama all the time  2013 also saw a pair of rom-com  supporting roles in the spectacular now  and don john  and in 2015 she charmed audiences with  her comedic chops and amy schumer's  train wreck  playing a fictionalized version of  schumer's sister kim and enduring a very  unusual audition process to land the  part  it all started when director judd apatow  called larsen and invited her to lunch  my agent is like what what happened what  did you do i was like i don't know i  just talked about myself for a while and  i ate a salad and that was sort of van  like what did they want i was like i  don't know  as she tells it larson came back for  lunch every day and soon bill hader  showed up too  apatow eventually filled the actors in  on his plans using the get togethers as  part of his unorthodox casting process  oscar winner after reading emma  donohue's book room in a single day  larson knew she wanted to play the part  of ma the kidnapped teen turned  long-term captive and mother  after beating out several other  actresses for the part larson dove into  the role with a massive amount of prep  work  she avoided the sun to achieve a palette  complexion packed on 15 pounds of lean  muscle  and even stayed home for a month an  experience she admitted was intensely  draining both physically and emotionally  larson's emotionally raw performance in  room was met with near universal acclaim  and earned her the biggest hollywood  accolade of them all an oscar  raising the stakes the claustrophobic  confines of room  were followed with a complete 180 for  larsen when she landed a main role in  2017's kong skull island  shot in vietnam in hawaii it was full of  big everything  big budget big a-list co-stars big  special effects and of course  one very big gorilla while her first  post-oscar performance wasn't received  with the same glowing critical praise as  past roles she was credited with turning  the franchise's traditionally fainting  female lead into a more modern  empowered counterpart to tom  hiddleston's explorer more importantly  kong skull island proved larsen had the  star power to carry a popcorn flick  it was her most successful box office  outing to date taking in 566 million  dollars worldwide  meet captain marvel at comic con 2016  the cast of the marvel universe  assembled on stage for a family photo  and then came a special announcement  brie larson was introduced as captain  marvel a role everyone at marvel takes  seriously you're gonna get the most  powerful superhero that we've ever  that we've ever introduced with i think  one of the most unique and inspiring  origin stories  that's an awful lot of responsibility  for one movie but larson seems eager to  step up to the challenge  she told reporters i'm really proud of  what it is that we're making  i think all the hype and anticipation  will be worth it  looks like a perfect fit

